<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40957" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕlēgātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		1. relego. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A sending away</i>, <i>exiling</i>,
				<i>banishment</i>, <i>relegation</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">atque amandatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rosc. Am. 15, 44</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">with exsilium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 3,
					10 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4,
			4</span></i>.— With <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insulae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Paul. Sent. 5, 4, 17</span></i>
			; v. 1. relego, I. A. 2.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A bequest</i>, <i>legacy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dotis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 33, 4, 1, § 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
